<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 23 May, from 1040 to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1040">1040 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">986 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Seljuks defeat the Ghaznavids at the Battle of Dandanaqan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merv">Merv</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Turks</a> won a decisive victory over the Ghaznavid army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mas'ud. The battle gave them control of Khurasan, opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> to them and marked the foundation of the Seljuk Empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dandanaqan">Battle of Dandanaqan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavid Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1308">1308 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">718 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce defeats John Comyn, Earl of Buchan, at Inverurie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a> defeated his chief domestic enemy, John Comyn, 3rd Earl of Buchan, at Inverurie in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Fordun dated the battle to May 1308, while Barbour placed it at Christmas 1307.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1430">1430 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">596 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is captured at Compiègne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leading a sortie from the besieged town, Joan was pulled from her horse by Burgundian troops. They sold her to the English, who had her tried for heresy and burned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a> a year later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1498">1498 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">528 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Girolamo Savonarola is executed in Florence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girolamo-savonarola">Girolamo Savonarola</a>, who had dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>'s restored republic after the Medici's expulsion in 1494, was hanged and burned in the Piazza della Signoria. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-vi">Pope Alexander VI</a> had excommunicated him in 1497, and he had lost popular support.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girolamo-savonarola">Girolamo Savonarola</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1618">1618 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">408 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Defenestration of Prague sparks the Thirty Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Protestant nobles threw two Catholic regents and their secretary from a window of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-castle">Prague Castle</a>; all three survived. The Bohemian revolt that followed grew into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1701">1701 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">325 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Captain William Kidd is hanged for piracy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kidd, commissioned as a privateer by English backers, was hanged at Execution Dock in Wapping. Many historians think he was made a scapegoat to protect his powerful sponsors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1788">1788 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">238 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">South Carolina ratifies the US Constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a> became the eighth state to ratify. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hampshire">New Hampshire</a>'s ratification a month later made nine, the number needed for the Constitution to take effect.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bonnie and Clyde are killed in a police ambush</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> lawmen shot Bonnie Parker and Clyde Barrow in their car near Gibsland, Louisiana. The pair's gang had killed at least nine police officers.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ben-Gurion announces the capture of Adolf Eichmann</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Israel's prime minister told the Knesset that Eichmann, a principal organiser of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>, had been found and was in Israeli custody. Mossad agents had seized him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li></ol>
